In earlier Spanish Nethacks, an invisible monster came up as "él" where the 
English would use "it": _Él te golpea_.  The latest version attempts to fix 
that, but a few instances may have slipped through.  It requires some 
structural change to the program to simply leave the subject out, and 
consequently capitalize the following word, rather than substitute a 
pronoun:  _Te golpea_.

I don't know of any bug that would cause a _trasga_ to suddenly become a 
_trasgo_ simply because she was invisible.  Something to check out in 
wizard mode, supongo.


