There's a 3.4.3-based Spanish Nethack now, maybe you missed the email?

I've had some ideas on fitting the code with a set of language backends that 
could handle the peculiarities of each supported language.  These, paired 
with something like GNU gettext, could bring some kind of i18n to Nethack 
at last.

We already have Japanese and Spanish, Chaos Master has proposed a Brazilian 
Portuguese version, and at various times interest has been expressed in 
German and Russian.


